"Both checks behaved exactly as the contract requires:\n\n```text\nvalid history  -> OK\ntampered history -> ['hash mismatch at 2 (history tampered)']\n```\n\nThis confirms the core invariant: **any mutation of a committed entry invalidates its hash**, so the history is tamper-evident even though the verifier only recomputes digests.\n\n## Contract summary & notes on the guarantees\n\n**What the binding establishes**\n- **Format** — `LogEntry` is a hash chain: `hash = H(index ‖ term ‖ prev_hash ‖ txn)`, rooted at `GENESIS_HASH`, indices contiguous from 1, terms non-decreasing.\n- **Interface** — one mutator (`submit`) plus committed-only readers (`read`, `read_range`, `watch`, `status`); idempotency keyed on `(client_id, request_id)`.\n- **Guarantees** — linearizability, total order, prefix consistency, committed-only visibility, atomic commit, at-most-once application, quorum durability, monotonic `commit_index`, tamper-evidence.\n\n**Two nuances worth flagging (not defects, but scope limits)**\n1. **Hash chaining proves integrity, not correctness.** The verifier rejects a rewritten entry, but an adversary who recomputes the entire chain from the tampered point forward would produce a self-consistent history. Detecting that requires an **external trust anchor** — e.g. periodic signed roots (Merkle/chain digest), or client-side pinning of a known `entry_hash` at a known index. Consider adding a `signed_root` field or a `get_root(index)` API if you need Byzantine tamper-resistance rather than crash-fault tamper-evidence.\n2. **`Receipt.timeout` means unknown, not failed.** The contract requires clients to retry timeouts with the *same* `request_id`; the service must then return `status=\"duplicate\"` with the original index/hash. This is what makes the durability + idempotency guarantees compose — the safety net only holds if both sides honor it. I'd recommend adding a `reconcile(client_id, request_id) -> Receipt | None` call so clients can resolve an ambiguous timeout without re-issuing the payload.\n\n**Suggested next steps if you want to harden it:** define the quorum `N` and durability target (e.g. `⌊N/2⌋+1` fsync'd), specify the `watch` cursor semantics on truncation/compaction, and add a length/checksum of the persisted log to `ServiceStatus` for cheap log-divergence detection. Want me to extend the binding with any of these?"